==Trivia==
*Ironically, he is known as "One Horn" in English, Japanese and Chinese, whereas he actually has '''two horns'''. He is correctly named '''Two-Horn''' in Korean.
*While his Japanese name, Ikkaku-kun (一角くん), literally translates to "One Horn-kun", it also sounds similar to ''ikaku'' (威嚇), meaning "threat", "threaten", or "intimidate". [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] is often considered a threatening or intimidating color, which may be why One Horn is red.
*[[Samurai Doggy]] is the only One Horn variant whose Japanese name isn't a pun.
*Unlike real rhinos, One Horn and most of his variants are rather slow, to the point where they never get to their objectives on time, a fact constantly mocked in their descriptions.
**Metal One Horn, in spite of his augments, is only so good at taking and dispatching calls.
**Cyberhorn learned about the Cats' invasion through internet. However, he was not fast enough to show himself in Into the Future Chapter 1 and debuted in Chapter 2 instead.
**Oldhorn is a fortune teller who attempts to forewarn others of future disasters with his ability to foresee what's yet to come. Unfortunately, they end up occurring before he has a chance to actually prevent them.
*Not counting [[Enemy Bases|enemy bases]] with 0 range, One Horn has the shortest range of any enemy, standing at a mere 40.

